      "math_academy_id": "q-36716",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,\\pi \\le x\\le 2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(\\pi /2)}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the right-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(\\pi /2)^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
